      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hollins was named after an official who worked for the Kaul Lumber Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollins%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sprang up when the Columbus and Western Railway reached the area in the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollins%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "John Kaul founded the Kaul Lumber Company in Hollins after buying the Sample Lumber Company in 1888.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollins%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Kaul Lumber mill burned in 1908 but was rebuilt the same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollins%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During its peak, Hollins housed a hotel, several general stores, three churches, a school, and a cotton gin.",
